<main class="site-page info-page about-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
        <p class="page-eyebrow">About the project</p>
        <h1>A personal game, shared and improved.</h1>
        <p>
            Lazy Eye Blocks is a falling-block game with independently adjustable color channels
            for the left and right eye.
        </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-layout">
        <article class="about-story">
            <h2>Where it began</h2>
            <p>
                The original Lazy Eye Blocks project was created by Sasha Gurevich, drawing on
                personal experience with amblyopia and an interest in dichoptic games. It made a
                free browser-based blocks game available to people who wanted to explore this kind
                of visual exercise.
            </p>
            <p>
                This edition carries that idea forward with a refreshed interface, adjustable tile
                balance, browser-saved settings, and clearer run statistics. The red and blue game
                channels remain central to how it works.
            </p>
        </article>

